Code Defence Intelligence Brief
Date: Wednesday, November 25, 2026
Series: Vol. 2, No. 315
Today's threat intelligence landscape for Wednesday, November 25, 2026 is headlined by CISA adding the Barracuda Email Security Gateway (ESG) command injection vulnerability (CVE-2026-126550) to the Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog, active zero-day attacks targeting a SonicWall SonicOS SAML authentication bypass (CVE-2026-98001) across Gen 6/7 firewalls and NetExtender SSL VPN gateways, and N-able issuing urgent security updates for a CVSS 9.9 remote command execution vulnerability (CVE-2026-118902) in N-central endpoint agents.
Strategic Highlights
 * CISA Adds Barracuda ESG Command Injection (CVE-2026-126550) to KEV Catalog: Directives from @Barracuda Networks, @CISA, and BleepingComputer confirm active wild exploitation targeting input parsing subroutines during automated attachment archive extraction. Threat actors transmit malformed email attachments with shell commands to gain root execution on edge email gateways, carrying a mandatory December 16 compliance deadline for federal civilian agencies.
 * Active Zero-Day Exploitation Targets SonicWall SonicOS SAML Auth Bypass (CVE-2026-98001): Advisories from @SonicWall and The Hacker News warn of active wild attacks targeting SAML single sign-on assertion parsing across Gen 6, Gen 7, and NSv firewalls. Remote adversaries transmit manipulated SAML responses to bypass multi-factor authentication and gain full administrative access to firewall web management portals and NetExtender SSL VPNs.
 * N-able N-central Agent RCE (CVE-2026-118902) Targeted in Widespread Scans: Reports from Dark Reading and SecurityWeek detail a CVSS 9.9 deserialization flaw in @N-able N-central endpoint agent communication subroutines. Unauthenticated remote threat actors transmit crafted RPC requests over TCP port 10004 to execute SYSTEM commands and drop ransomware across client endpoints.
 * LinkedIn Tags: Secure email gateway vendors, perimeter firewall developers, remote monitoring platform maintainers, and federal regulatory bodies managed by @Barracuda Networks, @SonicWall, @N-able, and @CISA are natively cross-referenced using assigned LinkedIn URN parameters.
